      "text": "To determine the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on two standard 6-sided dice is a prime number, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify all possible outcomes**: Each die has 6 faces, so there are \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\) possible outcomes when two dice are rolled.\n\n2. **List the possible sums**: The possible sums range from \\(2\\) to \\(12\\). We need to identify which of these sums are prime numbers. The prime numbers in this range are \\(2, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(11\\).\n\n3. **Count the number of favorable outcomes**:\n   - **Sum = 2**: The only combination is \\((1, 1)\\). There is \\(1\\) favorable outcome.\n   - **Sum = 3**: The combinations are \\((1, 2)\\) and \\((2, 1)\\). There are \\(2\\) favorable outcomes.\n   - **Sum = 5**: The combinations are \\((1, 4)\\), \\((2, 3)\\), \\((3, 2)\\), and \\((4, 1)\\). There are \\(4\\) favorable outcomes.\n   - **Sum = 7**: The combinations are \\((1, 6)\\), \\((2, 5)\\), \\((3, 4)\\), \\((4, 3)\\), \\((5, 2)\\), and \\((6, 1)\\). There are \\(6\\) favorable outcomes.\n   - **Sum = 11**: The only combination is \\((5, 6)\\) and \\((6, 5)\\). There are \\(2\\) favorable outcomes.\n\n   Adding these, the total number of favorable outcomes is:\n   \\[\n   1 + 2 + 4 + 6 + 2 = 15\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the probability**: The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of possible outcomes}} = \\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}\\).",
