      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on two standard 6-sided dice is a prime number, we first need to identify all possible outcomes and the favorable outcomes.\n\nThe possible sums when two dice are tossed range from 2 to 12. We will list all the prime numbers within this range: 2, 3, 5, 7, and 11.\n\nNext, we will count the number of ways to achieve each of these prime sums:\n\n1. **Sum = 2**: The only combination is (1, 1). (1 way)\n2. **Sum = 3**: The combinations are (1, 2) and (2, 1). (2 ways)\n3. **Sum = 5**: The combinations are (1, 4), (2, 3), (3, 2), and (4, 1). (4 ways)\n4. **Sum = 7**: The combinations are (1, 6), (2, 5), (3, 4), (4, 3), (5, 2), and (6, 1). (6 ways)\n5. **Sum = 11**: The combinations are (5, 6) and (6, 5). (2 ways)\n\nNow, we sum the number of favorable outcomes:\n\\[ 1 + 2 + 4 + 6 + 2 = 15. \\]\n\nThe total number of possible outcomes when two dice are tossed is:\n\\[ 6 \\times 6 = 36. \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is:\n\\[ \\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12}. \\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}. \\]",
